      "snowpackStructure": {
        "comment": "Snow cover is absent or patchy in many areas, up to the highest altitudes on the southern slopes; in general, the snowpack is increasingly thinning. Outgoing longwave radiation during the night will be quite good. The weather conditions as the day progresses will give rise to increasing and thorough wetting of the snowpack. In very isolated cases weak layers exist in the snowpack on shady slopes."
